# FreeCAD: always reload show model when edits finish

**Mandatory end-of-turn step** — do not wait for the user to ask.

Whenever this turn changes FreeCAD CAD (geometry, placement, materials, `show_jgb37_gui.py`, `.FCStd`, or related freecad scripts), before ending the turn:

1. Finish the code/model edits.
2. **Kill** all FreeCAD processes: `freecad`, `FreeCAD`, `freecadcmd`.
3. **Start-Process** FreeCAD with the show script (rebuilds + displays). Prefer the script over opening a stale `.FCStd` alone.

## Paths (this machine / repo)

- Script: `d:\Project\coutingmachine\3d_model\freecad\show_jgb37_gui.py`
- Doc: `d:\Project\coutingmachine\3d_model\freecad\out\jgb37_motor_bracket.FCStd`
- Exe: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\FreeCAD 1.1\bin\freecad.exe`

```powershell
Get-Process -Name freecad,FreeCAD,freecadcmd -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Stop-Process -Force
Start-Process -FilePath "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Programs\FreeCAD 1.1\bin\freecad.exe" `
  -ArgumentList "d:\Project\coutingmachine\3d_model\freecad\show_jgb37_gui.py"
```

## When it applies

- Any edit under `3d_model/freecad/`
- Any change that updates the FreeCAD model the user is viewing
- Even “small” tweaks (color, transparency, hole, dimension)

## When it does NOT apply

- Pure docs / git / non-CAD work with no FreeCAD model change
- User explicitly says not to reopen FreeCAD

Never leave a stale FreeCAD window as the user’s view of the model.
